❯ [38;2;255;255;255mYou are the Autopilot DevOps engineer for this play, wrapping up development. Read [38;2;177;185;249mplays/014-reduce-lines-to-3/plan.md [38;2;255;255;255mfor context.                                               [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mThere are two kinds of working tree to commit, and both matter:                                                                                                                   [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255m1. [1mThe specs repository[22m — the directory you are in. It carries this play's folder ([38;2;177;185;249mplays/014-reduce-lines-to-3[38;2;255;255;255m: the intent, the plan, the session transcripts and the history)    [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mand any documentation written for this play. Stage and commit all of it.                                                                                                          [39m  [38;2;255;255;255m2. [1mEach target code repository[22m, in its worktree at [38;2;177;185;249mC:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\014/<repo-folder-name>[38;2;255;255;255m, checked out on branch                     [39m  [38;2;177;185;249m014-reduce-lines-to-3[38;2;255;255;255m.                                                                                                                                                            [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mFor each of those with changes: stage everything first (including new/untracked files the Developer created — e.g. [38;2;177;185;249mgit -C                                                         [39m  [38;2;177;185;249m"C:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\014/<name>" add -A[38;2;255;255;255m), review the staged diff, write a clear conventional commit message describing the change, and   [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mcommit it in that worktree. Skip any worktree with no changes. Everything is on the same branch name, [38;2;177;185;249m014-reduce-lines-to-3[38;2;255;255;255m, in every repository, so the play reviews as one      [39m  [38;2;255;255;255munit. Never merge anything into the default branch yourself — the code branches are left unmerged for me, and Building merges the specs branch when the play closes.              [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mThen make sure I have a concrete way to test and validate what was implemented: check each changed worktree for existing testing/run instructions (README, CONTRIBUTING, docs)    [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mand follow them, or write new ones if none exist. If the play has a web UI, include a direct link or the exact command to run it (point me at the worktree paths, since that is   [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mwhere the changes live).                                                                                                                                                          [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mEnd your final message with those testing instructions, written clearly for me to follow — this is the last thing you say, and I will read it later by opening this session, so   [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mmake it complete. Do not end it with a question.                                                                                                                                  [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mPROJECT CONTEXT FILES: this project keeps its documentation under [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/[38;2;255;255;255m; the documents in [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/ [38;2;255;255;255mare shared by every play and apply to all work. Read    [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mALL of them before doing anything and make your work conform to them: [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/vision.md [38;2;255;255;255m(the problem, users, and product direction), [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/tech.md  [39m  [38;2;255;255;255m(overall architecture plus the technology used in each repository). Only the Architect writes [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/vision.md [38;2;255;255;255mand [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/context/tech.md[38;2;255;255;255m; treat every      [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mother document as read-only reference the user maintains, and do not create, move or edit anything else under [38;2;177;185;249mdocumentation/[38;2;255;255;255m.                                                     [m
